Bob wins if and only if the difference between the question marks on each side can exactly balance the current sum difference at an average contribution of 4.5 per question mark.
Solution & Intuition
 * Symmetry: If one side has more ? than the other by an odd count, Alice always wins because she gets the last move on that difference and can force an inequality.
 * Pair Strategy: For every pair of ? on one side, Bob can always ensure the pair sums to 9 (if Alice picks x, Bob picks 9 - x). Thus, each pair of excess ? contributes an expected sum of 9, or an average of 4.5 per ?.
